title: Army Committees
card-image: img/cards/military_policy.svg?v=2
subtitle: Discipline against the soldiers' trust.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: coalition_affairs
view-if: military_policy_timer <= 0 and at_war = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; military_policy_timer = 3

Order No. 1 gave the soldiers' committees power over their units. The army is held together by committees and by habit. (Army discipline: [+ army_discipline : level +].)

- @authority: Restore officers' authority; keep the committees only for supply.
- @trust: Trust the committees and send commissars to every unit.
- @death_penalty: Restore the death penalty at the front.
- @easy_discard

@authority

How should the party go about it? Cautiously, with compromises, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. In full, it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can carry it out and break its opponents.

- @authority_slow: Go about it cautiously, with compromises.
- @authority_decree: Carry it out in full.
- @authority_force: Carry it out in full, and break any opposition by force.

@authority_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
RO.add(Q, {army_discipline: 6, bolshevik: 2, right_threat: 2, rel_kad: 3});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: -3});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 1, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 2);
}, "Restore officers' authority; keep the committees only for supply");
!}

Officers regained their authority over operational orders. The committees have been told to concern themselves with food and boots. (It was done cautiously, with compromises.)



